From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:24:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 70/79] lanes: the thinking budget's cut waits for a tool
 result's forced rows

A request thinking_budget with a compute-lane call inside the reasoning failed the reply: the cut could land
inside the held result's forced rows (startClose cleared them, so the server saw a different result), or past
a drawn EOS in the same round (the stream then held with the close queued and resumeHeld asserted).

thinkCut now skips the commit's forced lead, waits while forced rows are queued and stops at a drawn EOS;
startClose appends its close and keeps resumed_rows. Replies without a lane call are unchanged.

Tests (test-budget-hold-host): a cut inside a held result, no lane call, a lane call after the close,
thinking off.
